## Designer Guides

### Intent

- Goal: Step-by-step learning paths for AI design tools — Claude Code, Cursor, GitHub Copilot, GitHub
- User: Designer or engineer picking up a new AI tool and wanting a structured way to learn it, not scattered YouTube tutorials
- Not trying to: Replace official documentation. Guides focus on design-relevant workflows, not comprehensive feature coverage.

### Interaction Model

1. User browses guides on /guides page. Featured guide (Claude Code) is highlighted as entry point.
2. Each guide has modules and lessons organized as a learning path.
3. Metadata (read time, lesson count, module count) helps users estimate commitment.
4. Guides cover practical workflows: setup, Figma-to-code, prototyping, version control, best practices.

### Not This

- These are not certification courses. No quizzes, no progress tracking, no certificates.
- These are not official tool documentation. They focus on design workflows, not every feature.
- There are currently 4 guides. Do not state a different number.

